When Tabular FM Wins

Choose TFM when you need:

1. Risk Scoring

Examples:

Fraud score
Credit score
Churn score
Customer lifetime value

Reason: The model needs to infer hidden patterns.

2. Forecasting

Questions like:

Will customer churn?
Will loan default?
Future sales?

RAG cannot predict unseen outcomes.

3. Anomaly Detection

Questions:

Is this transaction unusual?
Is this device abnormal?

Requires statistical learning.

TFM wins.

When RAG Wins

Choose RAG when you need:

1. Business Q&A

Examples:

Which products grew fastest in Q2?

What was revenue in ASEAN region?

No retraining needed.

2. Compliance and Audit

Questions:

Why was this customer rejected?

Which policy section applied?

RAG shines because answers require retrieving evidence.

3. Executive Dashboards

Questions:

Summarize the top fraud trends this month.

Compare Indonesia and Singapore fraud losses.

Much easier with RAG.

Biggest Mistake

Many teams try:

LLM + CSV


and expect:

prediction
classification
anomaly detection

LLMs are often poor at discovering subtle statistical patterns in raw tabular data.

Example:

Fraud signal may be:

Device Age < 2 days
AND
Velocity > 7 tx/min
AND
Merchant Category = X


A trained tabular model finds these patterns far better than RAG.

