For Your Fraud Analytics Use Case

Looking at roles like Fraud Analytics at banks (OCBC, Shinhan, etc.), I'd rank options as:

Use Tabular FM if:
Transaction-level fraud detection
Real-time risk scoring
AML anomaly detection
Account takeover detection
Use RAG if:
Investigator copilot
Fraud case search
Policy QA
Audit explanation
SAR/report generation
Use Both if:

You want:

"Score the transaction and explain why."

Example:

Fraud Probability: 92%

Retrieved Evidence:
- Velocity rule triggered
- Similar to 147 prior confirmed fraud cases
- Device fingerprint matches known risk cluster

Explanation:
The transaction was flagged primarily due to...


This hybrid "predict + explain" pattern is where most modern banking fraud platforms are heading because it combines the strengths of statistical learning and retrieval-based reasoning.
